run('jensen-huang', 'entities', 'Remarks on the China AI market (2025)', """
Speaking on a Tuesday in May 2025, Huang said China's artificial intelligence market would likely reach about $50 billion in the next two to three years and that being locked out of it would be a "tremendous loss."[N] He argued that selling into China would bring back revenue and taxes and "create lots of jobs here in the United States."[N] "We just have to stay agile," Huang told CNBC's Jon Fortt in an interview alongside ServiceNow CEO Bill McDermott, both executives appearing in Las Vegas for ServiceNow's Knowledge 2025 conference. "Whatever the policies are of the government, whatever is in the best interest of our country, we'll support," he said.[N]
""")

